         them): bodies named seg0..seg8 with seg0 the root; joints segA_to_B;
         motors motorA_to_B; one segN_site + segN_touch per body; torso_vel /
         torso_gyro / torso_accel on the root site.

         Morphology note: Gym's ant has four fixed "aux" hip-stub capsules as
         jointless child bodies. Those are folded INTO seg0 as extra geoms here,
         deliberately: it removes 4 jointless bodies, giving 9 bodies / 8 joints
         / 9 touch sensors, which makes the proprio width 65 and act width 8 -
         byte-identical to the two-arm rower's observation contract. A decoder
         or policy architecture sized for one fits the other exactly.

         mass_scale=27.5 relative to Gym's ant (density 5 -> 137.5, gear 150 ->
         4125, armature 1 -> 27.5, damping 1 -> 27.5), per the invariance rule
         in three_seg_worm.xml's header: density, gear, armature, damping scale
         together, which leaves the creature's own motion exactly invariant
         (F = ma) while bringing total mass to ~22 kg, the worm's class, so the
         ball momentum ratio carries over to the drills.

         Leg layout (top view), seg{i}=upper (hip seg0_to_i), seg{i+4}=lower
         (ankle seg{i}_to_{i+4}):
              seg2/6  +y  seg1/5
                  \\    |    /
              (x neg)  seg0  (x pos)
                  /    |    \\
              seg3/7  (y neg)  seg4/8       -->
